## Summary
The Trump Administration has proposed a new fee structure for H-1B visas, which are used by foreign workers in the U.S. This proposal, announced on August 25, 2026, aims to adjust costs associated with the visa program. It could impact employers and international employees, including those in medical research and healthcare fields.

## Key Points
- The Trump Administration is introducing a new fee for H-1B visas, indicating potential policy changes.
- The proposal was published on August 25, 2026, by Katherine Knott in Inside Higher Ed.
- H-1B visas are essential for importing skilled labor, which includes professionals in medical research and technology.
- The fee adjustment may influence immigration policies and affect business recruitment practices.


